---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Container from '../../components/ui/Container.astro';
import SectionBar from '../../components/ui/SectionBar.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="China KOL & KOC Influencer Agency | TheRedScroll"
  description="KOL and KOC campaigns on Douyin, RedNote, WeChat. Creator vetting, live commerce, campaign management. Fixed scope. Team in Shanghai."
>

  <!-- Hero — Dark hero banner -->
  <section class="relative w-full overflow-hidden bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
    <div class="relative z-[1] max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-[48px] max-[1024px]:px-[32px] max-[640px]:px-[20px] pt-[160px] pb-[96px] max-[640px]:pt-[112px] max-[640px]:pb-[56px] text-center">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[#CC3333] mb-[16px]">
        Influencer marketing
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-[#FFFFFF] text-[48px] max-[640px]:text-[28px] font-medium leading-[1.15] mb-[16px]">
        The right creator talking about your brand is worth more than any ad.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.7)] text-[18px] max-[640px]:text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.5] mb-[40px]">
        We find the right KOLs and KOCs, vet them, brief them, manage the relationship, and track what actually came back. From Shanghai and Hong Kong.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-[12px] flex-wrap">
        <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Book a call</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary-dark" href="#what-we-do">See what we do</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why influencer marketing is essential -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="max-w-[680px]">
        <SectionBar />
        <SectionHeading overline="The case for creators">Why influencer marketing is essential</SectionHeading>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          <p>
            Advertising puts your message in front of people. Influencer marketing puts your product in the hands of someone they already trust. Both matter. They do different jobs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px] mt-[32px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">It reaches communities, not demographics</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">A KOL's (Key Opinion Leader) followers aren't an age bracket. They're people who share interests, taste, and trust in that creator. When that person recommends a product, the audience responds in ways they wouldn't for a paid ad.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Conversion rates tend to be higher</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Brands using KOL collaborations on RedNote report conversion rates roughly 2.3x higher than traditional ad channels. On Douyin, KOL-driven product links consistently outperform brand-created ads in click-through and purchase rate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">The market is growing fast</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">The influencer economy is forecast to hit RMB 117 billion ($16.8 billion) by the end of 2025. Over half of advertisers already use influencer content. KOL seeding and KOL-led commerce are where the growth is concentrated.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">But it's incredibly time-consuming</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Finding creators, checking if their followers are real, negotiating fees, writing briefs, reviewing content, tracking results. A single campaign with 15 creators can eat up 100+ hours. Most brands can't do this well in-house.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- What we do -->
  <section id="what-we-do" class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px] scroll-mt-[76px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="What we do">KOL and KOC identification</SectionHeading>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[48px] max-[640px]:gap-[32px] items-start">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)] max-w-[680px]">
          <p>
            We maintain a database of creators across Douyin, RedNote, WeChat, Weibo, Bilibili, and Kuaishou. Every creator on our list has been checked for engagement authenticity, audience quality, content style, and brand fit.
          </p>
          <p>
            We use platform tools like Xingtu (Douyin) and Pugongying (RedNote) plus our own checks. We've come across accounts with 500,000 followers and a 0.1% engagement rate. That's an immediate no.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Campaign planning and briefing</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">
              Every campaign gets a brief. Objectives, key messages, content format, posting schedule, platform rules, do's and don'ts. We coordinate KOL posting schedules with your brand content calendar and any paid media running at the same time.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Negotiation and contracting</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">
              We negotiate rates, usage rights, exclusivity terms, and deliverables. Listed rates and what brands actually pay can differ by 15% or more. We know what things should cost and we negotiate accordingly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Live commerce, compliance, reporting — dark section -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="bg-[#1A1A1A] rounded-[12px] p-[48px] max-[640px]:p-[32px_20px]">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[8px]">Full service</p>
        <h2 class="text-[#FFFFFF] text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.25] mb-[16px]">From live commerce to compliance to reporting</h2>
        <div class="max-w-[680px] flex flex-col gap-[24px] mb-[32px]">
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
            Live streaming is a serious sales channel. A single session on Douyin or Taobao Live can move thousands of orders in a couple of hours. We coordinate host selection, product briefing, script development, real-time chat moderation, and post-session reporting.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[24px]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">Compliance and disclosure</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              Sponsored content on Chinese platforms is subject to advertising regulations. RedNote requires clear disclosure labels. Douyin flags undisclosed promotions. We make sure every piece of KOL content meets platform requirements and complies with relevant advertising rules.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">Performance tracking</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              Every campaign is measured. Impressions, engagement rate, click-throughs, conversions, cost per result. Post-campaign reports include who to keep working with, who to drop, and who's worth testing next time. We refine the creator mix based on data, not gut feeling.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">Live commerce</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              For brands with a Douyin Shop, we run sessions linked directly to your product pages. Host selection, product briefing, real-time chat, and post-session reporting. The commission model means your risk is partially shared with the host.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[#FFFFFF] mb-[8px]">Payment handling</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal text-[rgba(255,255,255,0.6)] leading-[1.5]">
              Negotiation, contracting, payment, tax documentation. You pay us. We sort out the rest with the creators and their MCNs. Flat fee, commission on sales, product exchange, or hybrid structures depending on the campaign.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- What is an MCN -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Industry context">What is an MCN?</SectionHeading>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[48px] max-[640px]:gap-[32px] items-start">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)] max-w-[680px]">
          <p>
            MCN stands for Multi-Channel Network. In practice, it's a talent management company for creators. MCNs sign contracts with KOLs and KOCs, then manage their content production, brand deals, and monetization.
          </p>
          <p>
            As of 2025, there are roughly 29,000 registered MCN organizations operating across the market. Chinese MCNs train creators, produce their content, manage supply chains for live commerce, and handle platform compliance. A lot of the biggest names on Douyin and RedNote were incubated by MCNs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px]">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Why this matters for brands</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">
              When you want to work with a mid-tier or top-tier KOL, you're almost always negotiating with their MCN. Knowing which MCN manages which talent and having a relationship with the right people makes the process faster. And cheaper, usually.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Our MCN relationships</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">
              We work with major MCNs across Douyin, RedNote, and WeChat. Those relationships mean faster response times, priority access to creators who are usually booked out, and pricing that's hard to get if you're reaching out cold.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- KOL/KOC pricing — RedNote -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Indicative pricing">RedNote / Xiaohongshu</SectionHeading>
      <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)] mb-[24px] max-w-[680px]">
        Rates depend on follower count, engagement rate, content format, niche, and exclusivity. These ranges reflect Q1 2026 benchmarks. Not quotes.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Nano-KOCs (under 5K)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥100 to ¥500/post, or product exchange only. Best for seeding campaigns that build search presence through volume.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Micro-KOCs (5K to 20K)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥500 to ¥3,000/post. High engagement rates. Great for authentic product reviews and organic buzz.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Mid-tier KOLs (20K to 100K)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥3,000 to ¥15,000/post. The sweet spot for most campaigns. Good reach, real credibility, and the cost per engagement usually makes sense.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Top-tier KOLs (100K+)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥15,000 to ¥80,000+/post. Beauty and luxury KOLs command roughly 50% more than other categories. Video notes cost 20 to 30% more than photo notes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Douyin pricing -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Indicative pricing">Douyin</SectionHeading>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Micro-creators (under 50K)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥1,000 to ¥5,000/video. Good for product demos and tutorials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Mid-tier KOLs (50K to 500K)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥5,000 to ¥30,000/video. Effective for brand awareness and driving Douyin Shop traffic.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Top-tier KOLs (500K+)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥30,000 to ¥200,000+/video. Campaign anchors. Often bundled with live commerce sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Live commerce hosts</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Base fee plus 20 to 40% commission on sales. A strong host can move tens of thousands of units in a single session.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- WeChat pricing -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Indicative pricing">WeChat</SectionHeading>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Official Account KOLs (articles)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥5,000 to ¥50,000+/article depending on average views. The rough benchmark is about ¥1 per view. The most expensive platform per impression, but the audience quality is different. The attention is deeper.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Channels KOLs (video)</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">¥3,000 to ¥20,000/video. Growing format. Less established pricing than Douyin but expanding quickly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- Case study -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[48px] max-[640px]:p-[32px_20px]">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.05em] leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[8px]">Case study</p>
        <h2 class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.25] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[24px]">RedNote KOC seeding for an Australian supplements brand</h2>

        <div class="max-w-[680px] flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          <p>
            An Australian supplements brand was entering the market with a hero product (collagen powder) but zero recognition. No social accounts, no search presence, no reviews. On RedNote, if your product doesn't show up when someone searches the category, it doesn't really exist.
          </p>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-stone)]">
            The brand had budget for a KOL campaign but needed search presence first. Without organic reviews already on the platform, even a great KOL post would feel like it came out of nowhere. Consumers would search the brand name, find nothing, and lose interest.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phase one (weeks 1 to 4): KOC (Key Opinion Consumer) seeding. We recruited 40 micro-KOCs in the beauty and wellness space. Each got a free product plus ¥300 to ¥800 per post. The brief was simple: share an honest review, properly disclosed as gifted.
          </p>
          <p>
            Phase two (weeks 5 to 8): KOL amplification. With 40+ genuine reviews now live and searchable, we brought in three mid-tier KOLs (50K to 120K followers) for sponsored video notes. We boosted the top-performing notes with Juguang ads to push reach beyond their organic audience.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Results grid -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-4 max-[640px]:grid-cols-2 gap-[24px] mt-[32px] pt-[32px] border-t border-[rgba(0,0,0,0.08)]">
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">36</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">KOC reviews indexed in RedNote search for "collagen powder" and related terms.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-vermillion)] mb-[4px]">380K</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Combined views across three KOL video notes.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">2,400</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Monthly brand searches on RedNote, up from zero.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[28px] max-[640px]:text-[22px] font-medium leading-[1.2] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[4px]">890</p>
            <p class="text-[13px] font-normal text-[var(--color-stone)] leading-[1.4]">Product inquiries through RedNote DMs. Brand moved to a monthly retainer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- How to get started -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="Get started">Ready to launch an influencer campaign?</SectionHeading>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 max-[640px]:grid-cols-1 gap-[16px] mt-[24px]">
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">01</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Book a 30-minute discovery call</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Tell us about your brand, your goals, and what you've tried so far.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">02</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Get a KOL/KOC recommendation</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Creator profiles, pricing, and campaign structure. Clear scope and fixed management fee.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[var(--color-rice-paper)] rounded-[10px] p-[24px] max-[640px]:p-[20px]">
          <p class="text-[12px] font-medium text-[var(--color-vermillion)] leading-none mb-[8px]">03</p>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">First posts within three to four weeks</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] font-normal leading-[1.5] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Brief, creator onboarding, content production, review, and publication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="mt-[96px] max-[640px]:mt-[64px]">
    <Container>
      <SectionBar />
      <SectionHeading overline="FAQ">Frequently asked questions</SectionHeading>

      <div class="max-w-[680px] flex flex-col gap-[32px] mt-[24px]">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How do you detect fake followers?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">We cross-reference follower counts against engagement metrics, comment quality, and audience demographics. A creator with 200,000 followers and 50 comments per post, mostly generic emoji, that's a red flag. Platform tools like Xingtu and Pugongying also provide authenticated data. After a few hundred campaigns you recognize the patterns quickly.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How many KOLs do we need?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Depends on what you're trying to do. Seeding campaign: 20 to 50 KOCs. Brand awareness push: 3 to 5 mid-tier KOLs. Hero product launch: one top-tier creator supported by 10 to 15 KOCs. We build the mix around your budget and goals.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Can we approve content before it goes live?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Generally yes. We share drafts or preview content before publication. Some creators resist heavy editing because it kills authenticity, and they're usually right. But key messages, compliance labels, and brand guidelines always get checked.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">What's the difference between KOL and KOC?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">KOLs are professional creators with large followings and polished content. KOCs (Key Opinion Consumers) are everyday users with smaller audiences who share genuine product experiences. KOLs drive awareness. KOCs build trust and search presence. Most campaigns need both.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">How long to launch a campaign?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Two to four weeks from brief to first post. That covers creator identification, outreach, negotiation, briefing, content production, and review. Seeding campaigns with KOCs move faster, sometimes one to two weeks.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Can influencer content be reused as ad creative?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Sometimes. Usage rights have to be negotiated upfront. Some creators include ad usage in their fee. Others want a separate licensing payment, which can add 30 to 50% on top. We sort this out during contracting so nobody gets surprised later.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">What industries work best?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">Beauty, skincare, and fashion see the strongest results because the creator ecosystem is the most developed. F&B, health and wellness, hospitality, and consumer electronics are close behind. B2B brands can also make it work, especially on WeChat and Zhihu, but the pool of relevant creators is smaller.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-[8px]">Do you handle payments to creators?</h3>
          <p class="text-[16px] font-normal leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-stone)]">The whole flow. Negotiation, contracting, payment, tax documentation. You pay us. We sort out the rest with the creators and their MCNs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

